From 641e7b11e990f9aefe5f06a8cc9c13d843ffaacf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PranaliD <pdeore@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:09:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use Cinder catalog info with service credentials

When cinder_store_* credentials are set, glance_store
always used Cinder's public endpoint and ignored
cinder_catalog_info and cinder_endpoint_template.
That works on DevStack, where public Cinder is on the
same host, but fails on Kolla when glance-api can only
reach the internal endpoint.
Passing those options through to cinderclient so the
configured interface or URL is used.

Carried from the upstream review
https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/glance_store/+/1004991
(patchset 3) while it is still under review. Drop this patch once
a Debian Salsa python-glance-store 5.4.x release contains the fix,
or when StarlingX moves to OpenStack 2027.1, whichever comes first.

Closes-Bug: #2166752
Change-Id: I443017789c9b474be923d16b7667db36f0d0a875
Signed-off-by: PranaliD <pdeore@redhat.com>

[Cherry-picked from openstack/glance-store to stx-openstack]
Signed-off-by: João Fonsaka <joaovitor.fonsaka@windriver.com>
---
